This project uses pnpm, so all instructions should read accordingly.

Stracker (Stock Tracker) is a private site. It checks stock prices each day, runs formulas, and produces buy-signal alerts.

Alerts are measured by P0, P1 and P2 where P0 is a must buy and the other two are early indicators. EOD is End of Day.

A public Google Sheet CSV lists tracked symbols and is used as the source of daily close prices (`GOOGLE_SHEET_CSV_URL`).

Hosting is Vercel (Next.js). Postgres is Neon. Crons are defined in `vercel.json`:
- `/api/cron/backfill` at `0 0 * * 2-6` UTC (5 PM PT Mon–Fri)
- `/api/cron/daily` at `0 1 * * 2-6` UTC (6 PM PT Mon–Fri)

The contents of the secret sauce formulas must always remain secret. Local formulas live in `lib/secretSauce.local.ts` (gitignored). Production uses `SECRET_SAUCE_MODULE_B64`. If unit tests cover formulas, those tests should also stay out of git.

Passwords, API keys, and connection strings belong in `.env.local` (local) or Vercel environment variables (production). Never commit them.

Drizzle tables: `symbols`, `symbol_data`, `alerts`, `track`, `application_reports`.
